\section{Mathematical Appendix}

\subsection{Ricci Tensor Decomposition}
The Ricci tensor is computed using the conformal metric $\tilde{\gamma}_{ij}$:
\[
R_{ij} = \tilde{R}_{ij} + R^{\phi}_{ij},
\]
where
\[
R^{\phi}_{ij} = -2\tilde{D}_i \tilde{D}_j \phi
- 2\tilde{\gamma}_{ij}\tilde{D}^k \tilde{D}_k \phi
+ 4\tilde{D}_i \phi \tilde{D}_j \phi
- 4\tilde{\gamma}_{ij}\tilde{D}^k \phi \tilde{D}_k \phi.
\]

\subsection{Hamiltonian Constraint}
The Hamiltonian constraint is enforced on the GPU tensor cluster:
\[
\mathcal{H} = \tilde{A}_{ij}\tilde{A}^{ij}
- \frac{2}{3}K^2
+ e^{-4\phi}\tilde{R} = 0.
\]

\subsection{Momentum Constraint}
\[
\mathcal{M}^i = \tilde{D}_j \tilde{A}^{ij}
- \frac{2}{3}\tilde{D}^i K = 0.
\]

These constraints are evaluated every timestep to maintain physical consistency.